f the game. It lost 39.6 points, and Black's lead went from -18.7 to +20.9. The engine's choice was C8. By the end Black had captured 15 stones and White none."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with D7, which lost 0.0 points and was the engine's own first choice. It kept the +20.9 lead intact (+20.8) at the moment a single accurate move mattered most."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberty count (flagging groups with 2 or fewer), and count.py only flood-fills empty regions to tally territory and area score for the current position. Neither chooses, ranks, or looks ahead at moves, so both are position inspection.", "stop": false}}